    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d244">

                <pb facs="0610" n="524" sameAs="frus:frus1873p1v1/pg524"/>

                <head>No. 241.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. <persName corresp="#p_HF1"
                            type="from">Fish</persName> to Mr. <persName corresp="#p_CEDL1"
                            type="to">De Long</persName>.</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1872-08-29"><hi rendition="#italic">August</hi> 29,
                        1872</date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 133.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Mr. Shephard’s dispatch of July 20, 1872,
                    relating to his refusal to render assistance or protection to the Peruvian bark
                    Maria Luz, was duly received. As that vessel was engaged in the coolie trade the
                    proceedings of Mr. Shephard, as reported in that dispatch, are approved.</p>
                <p>I am, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed><persName corresp="#p_HF1">Hamilton Fish</persName>.</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
